---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Button from "../../../../components/ui/button/Button.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Icon from "../../../../components/ui/icon/Icon.astro";
import InsertTaskFigure from "../../../../components/rex-actions/InsertTaskFigure.astro";
import Link from "../../../../components/ui/link/Link.astro";
import MarkdownH1 from "../../../../components/MarkdownH1.astro";
import Prose from "../../../../components/Prose.astro";
import TerminalCommands from "../../../../components/TerminalCommands.astro";

import { rexActions } from "../../../../config/rex-actions";
import { projectLinks } from "../../../../config/site";

const section = "grid gap-7 border-t border-pewter pt-8 pb-10 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-12";
const sectionHeading = "max-w-sm text-3xl leading-tight tracking-tight md:text-4xl";
const actionHeading = "mb-3 text-xl font-semibold md:text-2xl";
const sectionBody = "[&>:first-child]:mt-0";
---

<BaseLayout title='Rex actions' description={rexActions.description}>
	<div class='site-container py-8 md:py-12'>
		<Breadcrumbs />

		<section class='pb-9 md:pb-12' aria-labelledby='actions-heading'>
			<MarkdownH1 id='actions-heading'>{rexActions.title}</MarkdownH1>
			<div class='grid gap-7 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_1fr] md:items-end md:gap-12'>
				<p class='max-w-md text-lg leading-relaxed'>
					Two palette actions for <Link href={rexActions.site}>Rex</Link>. Zinn: New task files a task. Zinn: Insert
					task pastes one into the program in the pane, ready for you to send.
				</p>
				<div class='flex flex-wrap gap-3 md:justify-end'>
					<Button href='#installation' variant='solid' size='large'>Installation</Button>
					<Button href='#keys-and-arguments' variant='outline' size='large'>Keys and arguments</Button>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<div class='pb-10 md:pb-12'>
			<InsertTaskFigure />
		</div>

		<section id='actions' aria-labelledby='actions-list-heading' class={section}>
			<h2 id='actions-list-heading' class={sectionHeading}>The actions</h2>
			<Prose class={sectionBody}>
				<h3 class={actionHeading}>Zinn: New task</h3>
				<p>
					Asks for a title, then for a project from the list of your projects, and creates the task there. On macOS and
					Windows, a system notification names the new task. Elsewhere, or when the notification cannot be shown, the
					palette shows it. Closing either prompt creates nothing.
				</p>

				<h3 class:list={[actionHeading, "mt-10"]}>Zinn: Insert task</h3>
				<p>
					Run it from the terminal pane that should receive the task. It lists the 2,000 most recently active open tasks
					of all your projects, each with the first line of its description and its column. Filter by key or title and
					pick one.
				</p>
				<p>
					The task's key and title, a blank line and its description go into the program in the pane as one bracketed
					paste. Nothing presses Return, so you can edit the text before you send it.
				</p>
				<p>Nothing is pasted, and the action stops with a message, when:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>the pane has no running program,</li>
					<li>the program in the pane changed while you picked,</li>
					<li>the program does not accept bracketed paste,</li>
					<li>or the task text contains terminal control characters other than tab and newline.</li>
				</ul>
			</Prose>
		</section>

		<section id='requirements' aria-labelledby='requirements-heading' class={section}>
			<h2 id='requirements-heading' class={sectionHeading}>Requirements</h2>
			<Prose class={sectionBody}>
				<ul>
					<li>Rex with <code>rex.ui</code> prompts, which need control API revision 17 or later.</li>
					<li>The <code>zinn</code> command on the <code>PATH</code> of the Rex server or of your login shell.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					The actions run <code>zinn</code> where the Rex server runs, so they use the database that <code>zinn</code>
					<Link href='/docs/settings#choose-the-data-directory'>selects</Link> there. When the server's
					<code>PATH</code> has no <code>zinn</code>, they read your login shell's <code>PATH</code> once and use that.
				</p>
			</Prose>
		</section>

		<section id='installation' aria-labelledby='installation-heading' class={section}>
			<div>
				<h2 id='installation-heading' class={sectionHeading}>Install the actions</h2>
				<p class='mt-5 max-w-sm text-lg leading-relaxed'>
					Put the <code>zinn</code> folder beside your Rex <code>init.lua</code> and load it there.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class='min-w-0'>
				<Prose class={sectionBody}>
					<p>
						On macOS and Linux, this downloads the files into <code>~/.config/rex/zinn</code>, or into
						<code>rex/zinn</code> under <code>$XDG_CONFIG_HOME</code> when that is set:
					</p>
				</Prose>
				<TerminalCommands class='mt-6' label='Download the Zinn actions for Rex' commands={rexActions.commands} />
				<Prose class={sectionBody}>
					<p>Then load the actions in <code>init.lua</code>:</p>
				</Prose>
				<TerminalCommands
					class='mt-6'
					label='Load the Zinn actions in init.lua'
					commands={[rexActions.require]}
					showsPrompt={false}
				/>
				<Prose class={sectionBody}>
					<p>And reload the configuration:</p>
				</Prose>
				<TerminalCommands class='mt-6' label='Reload the Rex configuration' commands={[rexActions.reload]} />
				<Prose class={sectionBody}>
					<p>
						To load one action only, require it by name, such as <code>require("zinn.new_task")</code>. Run the download
						again to update the files. To remove the actions, delete the folder and the <code>require</code> line.
					</p>
					<p>
						The download fetches{" "}
						{
							rexActions.files.map((name, index) => (
								<>
									<Link href={`${rexActions.downloadBase}/${name}`}>
										<code>{name}</code>
									</Link>
									{index < rexActions.files.length - 1 ? ", " : "."}
								</>
							))
						}
					</p>
					<p>
						Rex's <Link href={rexActions.configDocs}>configuration reference</Link> says where <code>init.lua</code> lives.
					</p>

					<details class='mt-6'>
						<summary class='min-h-11 cursor-pointer py-3 font-mono text-xs'>Windows</summary>
						<p>
							On Windows, the folder goes in <code>%AppData%\rex\</code>. Windows 10 and later include
							<code>curl</code> and <code>tar</code>, so in Command Prompt this fetches the folder from GitHub:
						</p>
						<TerminalCommands
							class='mt-6'
							label='Download the Zinn actions for Rex on Windows'
							commands={[rexActions.windowsCommand]}
							showsPrompt={false}
						/>
					</details>
				</Prose>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section id='keys-and-arguments' aria-labelledby='keys-heading' class={section}>
			<h2 id='keys-heading' class={sectionHeading}>Keys and arguments</h2>
			<div class='min-w-0'>
				<Prose class={sectionBody}>
					<p>
						The actions come without key bindings. Bind keys to <code>zinn_new_task</code> and
						<code>zinn_insert_task</code> in <code>init.lua</code>:
					</p>
				</Prose>
				<TerminalCommands
					class='mt-6'
					label='Bind keys to the Zinn actions'
					commands={rexActions.bindings}
					showsPrompt={false}
				/>
				<Prose class={sectionBody}>
					<p>
						An action asks for nothing it is given as an argument. With <code>project</code>, Zinn: New task files the
						task there without asking:
					</p>
				</Prose>
				<TerminalCommands
					class='mt-6'
					label='Bind a key that files tasks in one project'
					commands={[rexActions.projectBinding]}
					showsPrompt={false}
				/>
				<Prose class={sectionBody}>
					<p>With <code>title</code> as well, it asks nothing, which suits scripts:</p>
				</Prose>
				<TerminalCommands class='mt-6' label='Create a task from a script' commands={[rexActions.scriptCommand]} />
				<Prose class={sectionBody}>
					<p>Zinn: Insert task takes <code>task</code> to paste that task without showing the list:</p>
				</Prose>
				<TerminalCommands
					class='mt-6'
					label='Bind a key that pastes one task'
					commands={[rexActions.taskBinding]}
					showsPrompt={false}
				/>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section id='calls-to-zinn' aria-labelledby='calls-heading' class={section}>
			<h2 id='calls-heading' class={sectionHeading}>Calls to Zinn</h2>
			<Prose class={sectionBody}>
				<p>
					The actions run <code>zinn</code> only when you use one. While they are unused they make no calls, so none that
					you did not trigger, in use or idle.
				</p>
				<p>
					Each use of Zinn: New task makes at most two calls, <code>project list</code> and <code>task create</code>, or
					only <code>task create</code> when <code>project</code> is given. Each use of Zinn: Insert task makes at most two,
					<code>task list</code> and <code>task view</code>, or only <code>task view</code> when <code>task</code> is given.
				</p>
				<p>
					Each call names its action in the <Link href='/docs/cli/identity#client-chains'>client chain</Link>, as
					<code>zinn-rex:new-task/&lt;version&gt;</code> or <code>zinn-rex:insert-task/&lt;version&gt;</code>.
				</p>
			</Prose>
		</section>

		<div class='flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-5 border-t border-pewter pt-6'>
			<a class='inline-flex min-h-11 items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs' href='/integrations/rex/theme'
				>Zinn theme for Rex</a
			>
			<a
				class='inline-flex min-h-11 items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs'
				href={`${projectLinks.github}/tree/main/integrations/rex/zinn`}>Actions source <Icon name='external-link' /></a
			>
		</div>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
